Greetings, adventurers! We hope you've been enjoying [i]Questlist[/i].

If you don't have the game yet, now it's a great time to purchase it! It will be 20% off for the two weeks of the Steam Summer Sales.

Today's small patch introduces the following bugfixes:
[list][*]Fixed a bug that would make the game crash against the Sandworm in the Southills. The bug triggered when the boss [spoiler]would hid underground, becoming impossible to target[/spoiler], all the adds were killed, and Sunny used an offensive brew. She won't be able to use offensive concoctions anymore;
[*]Fixed a bug with the 'three boulders, three switches' puzzle in the Emerald Maze 3;
[*]Fixed an animation to properly centering on the slime in the sewers;
[/list]

Thank you for playing!

Greetings! We hope you have been enjoying [i]Questlist[/i]. Today's patch includes the following:
[h3]Changes to NG+[/h3]
[i]Questlist[/i] was designed with replayability in mind. Routes are complete experiences from start to finish, but focus on one specific perspective or theme; some only include happy endings, other routes only include tragic endings, some have a mix. 
Playing multiple routes enriches the story by showing the full picture.

To make replaying the game more enjoyable, we introduced NG+ some weeks ago.
Today we want to make some changes to it that will make it even easier to replay the game:
[list][*]Level, skill and equipment inheritance[/list]You will be able to inherit Vera's level, Vera's skill levels (so you'll start with [i]Dangerous Lips++[/i], for example), gold and equipment. You'll inherit one of all the jewels you already own: if you have two of the same jewels (for example, two [i]Water Strikes[/i]), you'll only inherit one. The levels of party members will match Vera's.

[b]IMPORTANT![/b] Level and equipment inheritance is [b]not retroactive[/b]: you'll need to watch the ending credits at least once to unlock it. We hope this change will make it easier for players to focus on the multiple paths of the story.
[h3]Balance changes[/h3]
[list][*]Enemies have been made scarcer in some areas. Less enemies are required to complete certain quests. The EXP & items they reward has been increased;[/list][i]Developer's notes[/i]: the areas most affected were Ostmoor, the Southills, the highways and most caves; this should remove the feel of grinding.
[list][*]Lowered HP & damage of the first Raina fight on Easy and Normal difficulties;
[*]Further decrease of damage and Freeze chance of the last boss on all difficulties;
[*]The slot machines in the casino have been reworked to be much more generous;[/list][i]Developer's notes[/i]: Dice Delight is the best way to make tokens, but players seem to enjoy the slots a lot. We decided to adjust the winning chances to make the spins feel more rewarding.
[h3]Miscellaneous fixes[/h3]
[list][*]Added a pop-up after unlocking the monkey's boon;
[*]Fixed a bug that made party members leave with accessories;
[*]Sunny's unique accessories will now be removed once she leaves the party;
[*]Fixed a bug that caused a softlock if the second floor of Lovett's tower was accessed from the left hallway;
[*]Minor text fixes;[/list]
Thank you for playing!

Greetings, everyone! We hope you've been enjoying [i]Questlist[/i]!
Today's patch might be a small download, but it introduces a highly requested feature and a bunch of fixes. Read along for the full changelog!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34914700/776b09a701fe445e2fd2bac009e39a94fd81cd7c.png[/img]
Many players have requested New Game + and it's finally here. Here's how it works:
[list]
[*]NG+ will unlock after completing the game once. If you already saw the ending credits at least once, you're in luck: NG+ is immediately available for you;
[*]Starting a new game from the main menu will offer you a choice: you can either start a fresh new savefile or a NG+ savefile;
[*]You'll be asked to answer a couple of questions to determine the outcome of specific quests;
[*]All the quests of days 1 to 11 will be marked as complete (except the long-term ones), and the rewards will be in your bag;
[*]The party will start at lvl. 20 with a selection of decent equipment, and enough gold to purchase upgrades;
[*]Most of Vera's skills will be close or very close to their first upgrade;
[*]After a super brief story recap, you'll be able to see the date scenes of the route of your choice, then jump straight into the confession scene on day 11;
[/list]
[h2]What was that about trading cards?[/h2]
We are very excited to announce that Community Items will soon be available for [i]Questlist[/i]!
That means trading cards, badges, emoticons, profiles and... yes, we also went the extra mile and went for Point Shop Items! Two exclusive animated stickers will be released when they're ready. Which is [b]soonTM[/b]. Here's a little preview:
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/34914700/699471f6108c8e531c0a9ed397dcec19a211f0a9.png[/img]
[h2]Bug fixes and balance changes[/h2]
Thank you all for reporting any issues and giving us feedback!
[h3]Balance changes[/h3]
[list]
[*]We upped the escape rate to 100%. This should help against the enemies in the [spoiler]Rosedell Caves[/spoiler]. Their stats are untouched, but now you'll be able to run away instead of seeing the game over screen if you get unlucky;
[*]We slightly reworked Fear: characters cannot get chain-feared anymore, and they'll be able to perform actions in combat more often;
[*]The final boss is now a bit slower (giving you more chance to go first), will use [spoiler]Banish[/spoiler] less often, and will inflict Freeze less often;
[/list]
[h3]New content[/h3]
[list]
[*]Added voice acting to two boss battles in the Emerald Maze;
[*]Added voice acting to the boss of the 'Not my kind of spelunking' quest;
[*]Added a ! balloon to Mavis on day 12;
[*]Made unselected choices semi-opaque. This makes the selected choice pop up more;
[/list]
[h3]Bug fixes[/h3]
[list]
[*]Some typos & text running out of the textbox have been corrected;
[*]Passability in a lot of caves has been adjusted;
[*]Fixed a crash caused by a misnamed asset on day 13;
[*]Fixed shenanigans caused by the crystals in the third stretch of the Emerald Maze;
[*]Fixed a possible crash in the gallery;
[*]Fixed a softlock caused by the [spoiler]Jester[/spoiler] boss in Reniel's route;
[/list]
[h3]Merging of the live and BETA branch[/h3]
We decided to downgrade the framework used for everyone. 
"Wait, shouldn't you[b] up[/b]grade it?" I hear you say. 
Well... no. The live version uses a recent version that offers a slightly better performance, but also occasionally causes freezes, and we don't want none of that.
Downgrading the framework also allows [b]Windows 7[/b] users to run the game, which is now officially supported. Achievement popups work as normal as well now~

Greetings! We hope you've been enjoying [i]Questlist[/i].
We just released a hotfix to the live & BETA build of the game. Here's what changed:
[h1]Live branch[/h1]
[h2]Balance changes[/h2]
[list]
[*]Health potions now restore 50 more HP, and should feel more effective in the early game. [/list]
[h2]Bug fixes[/h2]
[list]
[*]The option to disable mouse input is now available from the main menu, and is OFF by default. This does not affect current savefiles;
[*]Fixed a softlock caused by the rafts in the sewers;
[*]Fixed Reniel automatically switching to Avenger stance against a normal difficulty imp;
[*]Fixed a softlock caused by a boulder in the third stretch of the Emerald Maze;
[*]Fixed an issue that allowed you to complete the 'Rumors of assembly' quest before unlocking it;
[*]Clarified what players need to do to complete the 'Not my kind of spelunking' quest;
[*]You can now access the VIP area of the Stout if you have the pass, regardless of story progression. You'll still need to talk with the clerk at the Guild Affairs Office to progress;
[*]Removed a dev-only shortcut to skip the cave underneath the spa;
[*]Fixed a softlock caused by Dana vibing outside of her house on Celia's day 19;
[*]Fixed CG 18 unlocking in Celia's route but not Lyra's;
[*]Fixed CG 11 not unlocking properly;[/list]
[h2]More changes[/h2]
We removed the forced conversion to .webp of our images. This will hopefully improve performance, but it makes for a [i]big [/i]download.
We also fixed a bunch of typos. Seeing those float around always makes us sad.
[h2]Troubleshooting[/h2]
A small amount of users have reported freezing. If you're one of them, you can do the following:
[list]
[*]Update your drivers
[*]Disable V-Sync
[*]You can try switching to the BETA branch
[/list]
[h1]What is the BETA branch?[/h1]
The BETA branch uses an older version of the framework that is compatible with Windows 7.
If you're experiencing freezes, it might be worth switching to the BETA branch!
It just received an update with all the above fixes, plus a further downgrade of the framework that should fix the disappearing textboxes / battler flickering.

Hey there, adventurers!
Today we updated the demo of Catgirl's Questlist with a big patch. Thank you all for the amazing support and enthusiasm regarding the demo!
[img]https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/34914700/961713fe0f1de1cc967dae782c5f21bfbb95bc3c.png[/img]
[list]
[*] We reworked all the skills behind the scenes. They look and feel the same, but the rework should prevent a rare, nasty crash to occur;
[*] Reworked Reniel's[i] Battering Ram [/i]and updated the skill description;
[*] Vera and Sunny now correctly change idle stance when they're near death;
[*] When Sunny joins the party, she comes with more Healing herbs;
[*] Fighting the Soldiers in Hard mode will have you fight the correct enemies. Previously, the Normal Soldiers would fight you on Hard mode;
[*] Made the fight with the Roc of prey in the Emerald Maze more challenging, and reworked one of its abilities;
[*] Fixed the passability in the Emerald Maze;
[*] Slightly increased the Sleep chance of the Shrooms in the Emerald Maze;
[*] When one of Vera's skills improve, she now says the correct thing;
[*] Increased the spacing between the buttons in the title screen;
[/list]
[h1]We're over 50% funded on Kickstarter![/h1]
Thank you everybody for the support!
We recently introduced physical rewards. [url=https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/rascaldevworks/after-i-met-that-catgirl-my-questlist-got-too-long/posts/2535020]Check them out![/url]
The Vera daki should be revealed after the weekend, together with a backer-exclusive preview of Dana's sprite!
